# Folder structure

Single-page Vite + React + TypeScript site. Use this layout. Add a folder only when a file belongs there.

```
src/
  assets/            imported images, fonts, icons
  components/
    common/          shared UI, one folder per component
    layout/          site chrome: header, logo
  features/          page sections: profile, skills, projects, contact
  pages/             route-level views (Home today)
  styles/            global CSS (globals.css, app.css)
  App.tsx            root shell
  main.tsx           Vite entry
```

- A new section of the page goes in `src/features/<name>/` with a PascalCase component and an `index.ts` that default-exports it.
- Shared UI goes in `src/components/common/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` plus `index.ts`.
- Header, footer, and nav go in `src/components/layout/<Name>/`.
- Global CSS stays in `src/styles/`. Keep class names and import order. Do not convert styles to CSS modules as part of a move.
- `index.html` stays at the project root. Vite serves it from there. Files referenced by URL stay in `public/`.
- The Cloudflare Pages API stays in `functions/`. Do not move it into `src/services`.
- Shared helpers go in `src/utils/` and shared hooks in `src/hooks/` once they exist.
